        <headline>Special Weather Statement issued September 26 at 6:52AM EDT by NWS Jackson KY</headline>
        <description>Mostly clear to clear skies and light winds has led to fog
developing mainly in the valleys. Some of this fog will be dense
and reduce visibilities to a quarter of a mile or less along
rivers, larger creeks, and area lakes.

Those traveling this morning, should exercise caution by slowing
down and being prepared for sudden changes in visibility. Allow
plenty of room between your vehicle and the one in front of you.
Use low beam headlights and allow extra time to reach your
destination.
</description>
